From: Project local maintenance <local-build@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL DRAFT] Bind tar ACL operations to admitted runtime descriptors
Forwarded: no
Status: SOURCE-ONLY; not compiled, packaged or security-accepted

For the pinned Linux/Trixie libacl2.4 toolchain. Preserve legacy libacl ABI.
Use current tar payload FDs, admitted constructor parent/object handles, and
separate actual delayed-directory identities. All four ACL operation families
use AT_EMPTY_PATH. No legacy pathname fallback. This does not attest atomic
special-node birth against arbitrary same-type hardlink replacement, nor fix
unrelated chmod/chown/xattr paths or all other whole-image ACL consumers.

